Falsifies `domain_name_system::proofs::the_name_decoder_is_total_and_in_bounds`.

The defect: the decoder no longer requires a compression pointer to point strictly backwards, so
a pointer to itself, or two pointers to each other, send it round forever on a reply any name
server (or anyone forging one) can send.

Expected to fail: the unwinding assertion, on a message whose pointer targets its own offset.

diff --git a/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs b/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
@@ -451,9 +451,6 @@
                 if resume.is_none() {
                     resume = Some(pos + 2);
                 }
-                if target >= fence {
-                    return Err(Error::PointerForward);
-                }
                 fence = target;
                 pos = target;
             }
